guide aurum-druid/sleeping-bag
title Aurum: early sleeping bag detour
faction Alliance
race NightElf
class Druid
levels 14-30
zone Westfall
category Exploration
folder Aurum - Optional detours
version 1
keywords sleeping bag,pvp,cozy,early
reward item 211527
why Optional level-14 travel for the sleeping bag; separate from the fastest main leveling route.

step Choose the optional expedition
  tip The quest chain opens at 14. This is an early-unlock choice for a PvP server, not a claim that the long travel is the fastest way to level 30. Bring a partner if possible, repaired gear, drinks and camping supplies. Keep your Hearthstone at Sentinel Hill for the return from Kalimdor. Retain your main Aurum chapter in another Polestar tab so you can resume it afterward.
  level 14

step Westfall: the first note
  tip Search the Burned-Out Remains at Alexston Farm. Take the Alliance version of the note quest. This quest sends you to southern Barrens; the other starting version is for the reverse direction.
  accept 79008 object 415107 lvl 14

step Druid shortcut to the northern coast
  zone Moonglade
  tip Cast Teleport: Moonglade, then speak to Silva Fil'naveth for the free Druid flight. In Rut'theran, take the known flight connection to Auberdine. This avoids walking back across the Eastern Kingdoms to find a sea crossing.
  teleport 18960
  talk 11800
  fly "Rut'theran Village" npc 11800
  fly "Auberdine"

step Southern Barrens: the matching remains
  zone The Barrens
  tip Travel south through Darkshore and Ashenvale into the Barrens. Avoid Horde settlements and guards; the required camp is in the south. The arrow marks the quest object, not a guarantee of safe travel at level 14. Inspect the matching remains, then take Stepping Stones from the Nailed Plank beside them.
  turnin 79008 object 415106
  accept 79192 object 417072 lvl 14

step Stonetalon: Pocket Litter
  zone Stonetalon Mountains
  tip Return north through the Barrens and take the road into Stonetalon. Find Pocket Litter at the marked camp. Follow the quest interaction rather than unrelated camping features nearby.
  turnin 79192 object 424005
  accept 79980 object 424005 lvl 14

step Stonetalon: the Mound of Dirt
  tip Search the nearby marked Mound of Dirt to finish Scramble and take Wet Job.
  turnin 79980 object 424012
  accept 79974 object 424012 lvl 14

step Hearth back to Sentinel Hill
  zone Westfall
  tip With Wet Job taken, use your Sentinel Hill Hearthstone. This removes the long return across Kalimdor. If your bind is elsewhere or it is still on cooldown, choose an available return route; do not change your bind to a different inn for this instruction.
  hearth "Sentinel Hill"
  fly "Stormwind"

step Loch Modan: the Carved Figurine
  zone Loch Modan
  tip From Stormwind take the Deeprun Tram to Ironforge, then follow Dun Morogh's eastern road into Loch Modan. Continue north to Stonewrought Dam and inspect the Carved Figurine. Do not jump off the dam. The normal route is used for the approach; any final structure/ledge access still needs a client check.
  turnin 79974 object 424007
  accept 79975 object 424007 lvl 14

step Arathi: Messenger Bag at Thoradin's Wall
  zone Arathi Highlands
  tip Continue via Dun Algaz into the Wetlands, north across Thandol Span into Arathi, then toward Thoradin's Wall in the northwest. These are dangerous, contested areas for a level-14 character. The destination is the Messenger Bag at the wall, not the bridge at Thandol Span. Inspect the wall's access route carefully rather than jumping blindly.
  turnin 79975 object 406918
  accept 79976 object 406918 lvl 14

step Claim the sleeping bag
  tip Finish at the Hastily Rolled-Up Satchel near the Messenger Bag, then verify Cozy Sleeping Bag is in your bags. Use the item during natural waits. Its effect is separate from a Leatherworking tent's rested-XP top-up. Switch back to the Aurum leveling chapter you left; this optional guide does not replace that route or assume you completed unrelated quests.
  turnin 79976 object 424006
  collect 211527 x1 @22.45,24.21
